{
 "name": "seesaw_lowbat",
 "description": "Seesaw L1 car, short: narrow-track 4WD, one L motor direct on each axle (62 mm tyres inside the 64 mm\nplank), wheelbase 64 mm on one-piece 1x16 side beams. The battery box rides crosswise on a deck carried by\nthree-brick stacks on the beams, above the tyres, so the short car keeps weight on its front axle while the two\npassive 36.87 deg wedge arms (13-hole liftarms, low end C = (32, ZA-16) on T drop links) press the raised near\nend of the plank down to ~10 mm. The rear motor is held by an outboard T liftarm so no part origin lies behind\nthe rear axle (the goal is judged on part origins).",
 "chassis": "beam_l",
 "motor": "motor_f",
 "battery": "battery",
